Description: network mount manager for NFS, SMB/CIFS and SSHFS
 MountBridge is a GTK3 desktop application, designed for Xfce, for managing
 network mounts. It mounts NFS exports, SMB/CIFS shares and SSHFS
 connections, keeps passwords in the system keyring, shows mounts made
 outside the application, and can discover SMB and NFS servers on the
 local network.
 .
 NFS and SMB mounts go through a small validating root helper that members
 of the "mountbridge" group may run via sudo. To give a user access, run
 "adduser <user> mountbridge". SSHFS mounts need no privileges.
